🚩 Pacific War 1: Tactical Scenario Guide
This guide breaks down common combat "puzzles" you will encounter during a campaign and the optimal sequence of actions to solve them.

Scenario A: The "Invisible" Battleship
The Situation: You are taking heavy damage from a long-range Battleship, but you only see a ? ghost on your radar. You are in a FOG or TYPHOON.

The Counter-Play:

Do not fire blindly with your Battleship yet; you’ll waste precious ammo on a low-probability shot.

Maneuver your Destroyer at full speed (3 tiles) toward the last known ? location.

Activate Sonar Ping. This converts the ghost into a hard X target.

Identify: If the Destroyer gets within 2 tiles (or 1 in fog), the enemy HP is revealed.

The Strike: Now that the target is locked, fire your Battleship. Since the target is "spotted," your hit chance is calculated normally despite the weather.

Scenario B: The "Island Camper"
The Situation: An enemy Cruiser is "peeking"—moving out from behind an island, firing, and moving back, preventing you from getting a Line of Sight (LOS) on your turn.

The Counter-Play:

Launch a Torpedo with your Submarine or Destroyer aimed at the empty water next to the island where the enemy peeks.

The Dilemma: On the next turn, the AI sees the T (Torpedo) icon. To avoid a potential 10% instant-kill detonation, the AI is forced to move away from the island cover.

The Ambush: Position your Cruiser (Speed 2) to intercept the enemy's escape route. Once they are in open water, they lose their cover bonus.

Scenario C: The "Last Stand" Repair
The Situation: Your Battleship is at 25% HP and is currently Suppressed (Range reduced). An enemy Destroyer is closing in for a finish.

The Counter-Play:

Stop moving immediately. You need to start the 3-turn "Stationary" clock.

Screening: Move your Cruiser or Submarine directly between the damaged Battleship and the attacker. You are using the healthy ship as a "Human Shield."

The Turnaround: After 3 turns of cover, your Battleship hits Repair Tier 1 (+20 HP). This often brings you back above the "Suppression Threshold," allowing you to return fire with full 10-tile range.

Scenario D: The Carrier Hunt
The Situation: You’ve sunk the enemy screen, but their Carrier is still launching Air Recon, keeping your fleet constantly "Identified" (giving the AI an accuracy boost).

The Counter-Play:

Triangulation: Look at where the Air Recon 5×5 grid appears. The enemy Carrier must be within 15 tiles of that center point.

High-Speed Dash: Send your Destroyer on a flanking route along the edge of the map.

The Citadel Gamble: Carriers have 100 HP. A single Citadel Hit from a Battleship (max 180 damage) or a lucky Torpedo can sink it instantly. Do not trade shots; go for the "one-shot" kill to blind the enemy fleet.

💡 Summary of Tactical Symbols
Symbol	Meaning	Action Required
#	Island	Use as cover; cannot shoot through.
T	Torpedo	EVADE. Move at least 1 tile away from its path.
X	Active Contact	Optimal target for your main guns.
?	Ghost Contact	Use Sonar or move closer to re-acquire.
